%U A396596 110880,166320,221760,277200,332640,360360,498960,554400,665280,720720,1081080,1441440,2162160,2882880,3603600,4324320
%N A396596 Natural numbers k such that the sum of the x-th powers of the divisors of k achieves a record, for some x <= 0.
%C A396596 This sequence includes the highly composite numbers (A002182) for which x = 0; the superabundant numbers (A004394) for which x = -1; and the deeply composite numbers (A095848) for which x << 0. We note that superabundant numbers less than 10^11 are either highly composite or deeply composite, or both. We conjecture that the present sequence can be constructed simply as a union of highly composite numbers and deeply composite numbers. All terms must be the least of their prime signature (A025487). The intersection of the above sequences is A095849.
%H A396596 Hal M. Switkay, <a href="/A396596/b396596.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..98</a>
%e A396596 36 is a term in this sequence as it is highly composite (x = 0), even though it is not deeply composite.
%e A396596 420 is a term in this sequence as it is deeply composite (x << 0), even though it is not highly composite.
%Y A396596 Cf. A002182, A004394, A025487, A095848, A095849.
%K A396596 nonn,new
%O A396596 1,2
